  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 758886,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## Nord and Bert Couldn't Make Head or Tail of It: A Synopsis\n\nStep into the bizarre town of Punster in *Nord and Bert Couldn't Make Head or Tail of It*, a unique 1987 interactive fiction game from Infocom. This twenty-seventh release from the legendary company departs from their traditional fantasy adventures, challenging players with a series of wordplay puzzles unlike anything seen before. \n\nThe game is structured as eight independent \"short stories,\" each dedicated to a different style of wordplay, from homonyms in a grocery store (\"The Shopping Bizarre\") to literal interpretations of clichés on a farm (\"Buy the Farm\").  A quirky narrative thread connects these sections: idioms and clichés have manifested literally, and it's up to the player to restore order. \n\nUtilize the \"Jack of All Traits\" gadget, navigate a 1950s sitcom, and even appease a murderous chef – all through clever linguistic manipulation.  The final chapter, \"Meet the Mayor,\" requires mastery of the preceding sections, demanding players recall and apply solutions hinted at throughout the game.  Included with the game is \"Home on the Range,\" a booklet of wordplay-themed cartoons illustrating the game's whimsical puzzles. Prepare"
    },
